  {
   "id": "642168",
   "name": "Will Reichard",
   "pos": "PK",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-12T15:13Z",
   "shortComment": "Reichard made all three of his field-goal attempts and both extra-point tries during the Vikings' 23-13 win over the Saints on Sunday.",
   "longComment": "Reichard got the Vikings on the board early in the first quarter on a 40-yard field goal before connecting on kicks from 54 and 55 yards in the second and fourth quarter, respectively. Reichard has made at least three field goals in each of his last four games and is 15-for-15 on field-goal tries through five games, which is second-best in the NFL behind Spencer Shrader (16-for-16). Reichard is also one of five kickers who have made at least five field goals from 50-plus yards. The Vikings will be on a bye for Week 6 before welcoming in the Colts for Week 7 on Sunday, Oct. 25.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642013",
   "name": "Kyler Murray",
   "pos": "QB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T21:32Z",
   "shortComment": "Murray completed 24 of 30 passes for 229 yards with a touchdown and no interceptions while adding 10 rushes for 51 yards in the Vikings' 23-13 win over the Saints on Sunday. He also recovered a fumble.",
   "longComment": "Murray completed a season-high 80.0 percent of his passes while patiently carving up the Saints defense Sunday, and the returning Justin Jefferson unsurprisingly accounted for a significant chunk of the quarterback's production through the air with a 6-79-1 line on seven targets. Murray's yardage total was his second-highest of the season as well, trailing only the 247 he generated against the Dolphins in Week 4. The 2019 first overall pick may be starting to hit his stride in head coach Kevin O'Connell's offense, and he'll look to further master the scheme during a Week 6 bye before returning to action in a Week 7 home matchup against the Colts on Sunday, Oct. 25.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642011",
   "name": "Aaron Jones Sr.",
   "pos": "RB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T21:26Z",
   "shortComment": "Jones rushed 25 times for 113 yards and a touchdown and brought in all three targets for four yards in the Vikings' 23-13 win over the Saints on Sunday.",
   "longComment": "Jones continued handling the workhorse role in Minnesota's backfield, and he finished Sunday's contest with a new season high in carries despite exiting the game for a spell due to a leg issue. Jones added his second rushing touchdown of the season on an eight-yard run early in the fourth quarter, while the 100-yard effort was his second of the campaign. Sunday marked Jones' backfield mate Jordan Mason's fourth absence while on injured reserve due to a thumb injury, and it remains to be seen if the latter will be ready to suit up and put a dent in Jones' opportunities during a Week 7 home matchup against the Colts on Sunday, Oct. 25, following a Week 6 bye.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641996",
   "name": "Justin Jefferson",
   "pos": "WR",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T20:27Z",
   "shortComment": "Jefferson (ankle) brought in six of seven targets for 79 yards and a touchdown and rushed once for minus-11 yards in the Vikings' 23-13 win over the Saints on Sunday. He also committed a fumble that remained with Minnesota.",
   "longComment": "Making his return from a one-game absence due to an ankle injury, Jefferson capitalized on an opportunity to perform in front of his home-state crowd. The perennial Pro Bowler was expected to be busy due to Jordan Addison's (hamstring) inactive status, and Jefferson ultimately led the Vikings across the board in receptions, receiving yards and targets. The veteran receiver added his first touchdown since Week 1 when he recorded an impressive 15-yard scoring grab in the back corner of the end zone to cap off the first possession of the second half, and Jefferson will next set his sights on a vulnerable Colts defense in a Week 7 home matchup on Sunday, Oct. 25 following a Week 6 bye.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641923",
   "name": "T.J. Hockenson",
   "pos": "TE",
   "status": "Questionable",
   "date": "2026-10-11T17:42Z",
   "shortComment": "The Vikings downgraded Hockenson to out for Sunday's game against the Saints due to a concussion.",
   "longComment": "After recording a seven-yard reception on the Vikings' opening possession, Hockenson immediately headed to the locker room to get checked for a head injury. With Minnesota confirming that he has sustained a concussion, Hockenson will be shut down for the rest of the afternoon and will now be subject to the NFL's five-step protocol. Minnesota is on bye in Week 6, so Hockenson's next chance to play will come against the Colts on Oct. 25.",
   "details": {
    "fantasyStatus": {
     "description": "QUESTIONABLE",
     "abbreviation": "QUESTIONABLE"
    },
    "type": "Concussion",
    "location": "Head",
    "detail": "Concussion",
    "side": "Not Specified",
    "returnDate": "2026-10-25"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "641913",
   "name": "Michael Jurgens",
   "pos": "C",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T16:56Z",
   "shortComment": "Jurgens (elbow) is active for Sunday's game against the Saints, Craig Peters of the Vikings' official site reports.",
   "longComment": "Jurgens was activated from IR on Saturday. The offensive lineman has recovered from his elbow injury and is all set to suit up for Sunday's game.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641912",
   "name": "Brian O'Neill",
   "pos": "OT",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T16:54Z",
   "shortComment": "O'Neill (knee) is active for Sunday's game against the Saints, Craig Peters of the Vikings' official site reports.",
   "longComment": "O'Neill was limited in practice all week with a knee injury but has recovered enough to suit up for Sunday's contest.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641891",
   "name": "Ben Yurosek",
   "pos": "TE",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T16:20Z",
   "shortComment": "Yurosek (ankle) is listed as active for Sunday's game against the Saints, Craig Peters of the Vikings' official site reports.",
   "longComment": "Yurosek was activated from the Vikings' injured reserve Saturday, just in time for Week 5. The 24-year-old has yet to play in the 2026 season. He is expected to add depth behind T.J. Hockenson and Gavin Bartholomew versus the Saints.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641484",
   "name": "Brett Thorson",
   "pos": "P",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-09T01:10Z",
   "shortComment": "Thorson (hamstring) was a full participant in practice Wednesday and Thursday.",
   "longComment": "Thorson missed Sunday's Week 4 win over Miami due to his hamstring injury. However, with a pair of full practices to begin Week 5 prep, he's probably good to go for Week 5 versus New Orleans. Thorson should thus reclaim his role as the Vikings' punter.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641124",
   "name": "Blake Cashman",
   "pos": "LB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-07T01:04Z",
   "shortComment": "Cashman recorded eight tackles (three solo) and a fumble recovery during Sunday's 15-10 win versus the Dolphins.",
   "longComment": "In a game where Miami's offense simply couldn't stay on the field, Cashman only played 38 defensive snaps. Nevertheless, he managed to rack up seven-plus tackles for his 15th straight contest going back to last season. He's a solid IDP consideration in most formats going into a Week 5 tilt at New Orleans.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641113",
   "name": "Donovan Jackson",
   "pos": "G",
   "status": "Injured Reserve",
   "date": "2026-10-07T00:34Z",
   "shortComment": "Jackson (knee) was placed on injured reserve by the Vikings on Tuesday.",
   "longComment": "Jackson suffered a torn meniscus during Sunday's 15-10 win over Miami, and he was already set to miss the rest of the regular season, so Tuesday's move to the IR comes as no surprise. Joe Huber is the top candidate to take over as Minnesota's starting left guard in Jackson's absence.",
